{
  "title": "25: Al-Furqan الفرقان",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ الْفُرْقَانَ عَلٰى عَبْدِهٖ لِيَكُوْنَ لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ نَذِيْرَا ۙ‏(1)\nTABAARAKAL LAZEE NAZZALAL FURQAANA A’LAA A’BDEHI LE-YAKOONA LIL-A’ALAMEENA NAZEERAA.\nBlessed is He who sent down the Criterion to His servant that he may be a warner to all the nations.\nاۨلَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِى الْمُلْكِ وَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ فَقَدَّرَهٗ تَقْدِيْرًا‏(2)\nLAZEE LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LAM YATTAKHIZ WALADANW WA LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL MULKE WA KHALAQA KULLA SHAY-IN FA-QADDARAHU TAQDEERAA.\nHe, to whom belongs the sovereignty of the heavens and the earth, and who did not take any offspring, nor has He any partner in sovereignty, and He created everything and determined it in a precise measure.\nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً لَّا يَخْلُقُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَ وَلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لِاَنْفُسِهِمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا وَّلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مَوْتًا وَّلَا حَيٰوةً وَّلَا نُشُوْرًا‏(3)\nWAT TAKHAZOO MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAL LAA YAKHLOQOONA SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA WA LAA YAMLEKOONA LE-ANFOSEHIM ZARRANW WA LAA NAF-A’NW WA LAA YAMLEKOONA MAWTANW WA LAA HAYAATANW WA LAA NOSHOORAA.\nYet they have taken gods besides Him who create nothing and have themselves been created, and who have no control over their own harm or benefit and have no control over [their own] death, life, or resurrection.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِفْكٌ اۨفْتَرٰٮهُ وَاَعَانَهٗ عَلَيْهِ قَوْمٌ اٰخَرُوْنَ‌‌ ۛۚ فَقَدْ جَآءُوْ ظُلْمًا وَّزُوْرًا ۛۚ‏(4)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA IFKONIF TARAAHO WA A-A’ANAHU A’LAYHE QAWMUN AAKHAROON, FAQAD JAAA-OO ZULMANW WA ZOORAA.\nThe faithless say, ‘This is nothing but a lie that he has fabricated, and other people have abetted him in it.’ Thus they have certainly come out with wrongdoing and falsehood.\nوَقَالُوْۤا اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ اكْتَتَبَهَا فَهِىَ تُمْلٰى عَلَيْهِ بُكْرَةً وَّاَصِيْلًا‏(5)\nWA QAALOO ASAATEERUL AWWALEENAK TATABAHAA FAHEYA TUMLAA A’LAYHE BUKRATANW WA ASEELAA.\nThey say, ‘He has taken down myths of the ancients, and they are dictated to him morning and evening.’\nقُلْ اَنْزَلَهُ الَّذِىْ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(6)\nQUL ANZALAHUL LAZEE YA’LAMUS SIRRA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, INNAHU KAANA GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nSay, ‘It has been sent down by Him who knows the hidden in the heavens and the earth. Indeed He is all-forgiving, all-merciful.’\nوَقَالُوْا مَالِ هٰذَا الرَّسُوْلِ يَاْكُلُ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشِىْ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مَلَكٌ فَيَكُوْنَ مَعَهٗ نَذِيْرًا ۙ‏(7)\nWA QAALOO MAALE HAAZAR RASOOLE YAAKOLUT TA-A’AMA WA YAMSHEE FIL ASWAAQ, LAWLAA UNZELA ELAYHE MALAKUN FA-YAKOONA MA-A’HU NAZEERAA.\nAnd they say, ‘What sort of apostle is this who eats food and walks in the marketplaces? Why has not an angel been sent down to him so as to be a warner along with him?’\nاَوْ يُلْقٰٓى اِلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ جَنَّةٌ يَّاْكُلُ مِنْهَا‌ ؕ وَقَالَ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا رَجُلًا مَّسْحُوْرًا‏(8)\nAW YULQAA ELAYHE KANZUN AW TAKOONO LAHU JANNATUN-Y YAAKOLO MINHAA, WA QAALAZ ZAALEMOONA IN TATTABE-O’ONA ILLAA RAJOLAM MASHOORAA.\nOr, ‘[Why is not] a treasure thrown to him, or [why does] he [not] have a garden from which he may eat?’ And the wrongdoers say, ‘You are just following a bewitched man.’\nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ ضَرَبُوْا لَكَ الْاَمْثَالَ فَضَلُّوْا فَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ سَبِيْلاً‏(9)\nUNZUR KAYFA ZARABOO LAKAL AMSAALA FA-ZALLOO FALAA YASTATEE-O’ONA SABEELAA.\nLook, how they coin epithets for you; so they go astray, and cannot find the way.\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ جَعَلَ لَكَ خَيْرًا مِّنْ ذٰ لِكَ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ۙ وَيَجْعَلْ لَّكَ قُصُوْرًا‏(10)\nTABAARAKAL LAZEE IN SHAAA-A JA-A’LA LAKA KHAYRAM MIN ZAALEKA JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO, WA YAJ-A’L LAKA QOSOORAA.\nBlessed is He who will grant you better than that if He wishes—gardens with streams running in them, and He will make for you palaces.\nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالسَّاعَةِ‌ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِمَنْ كَذَّبَ بِالسَّاعَةِ سَعِيْرًا‌ ۚ‏(11)\nBAL KAZZABOO BIS-SAA-A’H, WA A-A’TADNAA LEMAN KAZZABA BIS-SAA-A’TE SA-E’ERAA.\nIndeed, they deny the Hour, and We have prepared a Blaze for those who deny the Hour.\nاِذَا رَاَتْهُمْ مِّنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ سَمِعُوْا لَهَا تَغَيُّظًا وَّزَفِيْرًا‏(12)\nEZAA RA-ATHUM MIM MAKAANIM BA-E’EDIN SAME-O’O LAHAA TAGHAYYOZANW WA ZAFEERAA.\nWhen it sights them from a distant place, they will hear it raging and roaring.\nوَاِذَاۤ اُلْقُوْا مِنْهَا مَكَانًا ضَيِّقًا مُّقَرَّنِيْنَ دَعَوْا هُنَالِكَ ثُبُوْرًا ؕ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ULQOO MINHAA MAKAANAN ZAYYEQAM MOQARRANEENA DA-A’W HONAALEKA SOBOORAA.\nAnd when they are cast into a narrow place in it, bound together [in chains], they will pray for [their own] annihilation.\nلَا تَدْعُوا الْيَوْمَ ثُبُوْرًا وَّاحِدًا وَّادْعُوْا ثُبُوْرًا كَثِيْرًا‏(14)\nLAA TAD-U’L YAWMA SOBOORANW WAAHEDANW WAD O’O SOBOORAN KASEERAA.\n[They will be told:] ‘Do not pray for a single annihilation today, but pray for many annihilations!’\nقُلْ اَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ اَمْ جَنَّةُ الْخُلْدِ الَّتِىْ وُعِدَ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ ‌ؕ كَانَتْ لَهُمْ جَزَآءً وَّمَصِيْرًا‏(15)\nQUL AZAALEKA KHAYRUN AM JANNATUL KHULDIL LATEE WO-E’DAL MUTTAQOON, KAANAT LAHUM JAZAAA-ANW WA MASEERAA.\nSay, ‘Is that better, or the everlasting paradise promised to the Godwary, which will be their reward and destination?’\nلَّهُمْ فِيْهَا مَا يَشَآءُوْنَ خٰلِدِيْنَ‌ ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ وَعْدًا مَّسْئُوْلًا‏(16)\nLAHUM FEEHAA MAA YASHAAA-OONA KHAALEDEEN, KAANA A’LAA RABBEKA WA’DAM MAS-OOLAA.\nThere they will have whatever they wish, abiding [forever]—a promise [much] besought, [binding] on your Lord.\nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَيَقُوْلُ ءَاَنْتُمْ اَضْلَلْتُمْ عِبَادِىْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اَمْ هُمْ ضَلُّوا السَّبِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHOROHUM WA MAA YA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE FA-YAQOOLO A-ANTUM AZLALTUM E’BAADEE HAA-OLAAA-E AM HUM ZALLUS SABEEL.\nOn the day that He will muster them and those whom they worship besides Allah, He will say, ‘Was it you who led astray these servants of Mine, or did they themselves stray from the way?’\nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ مَا كَانَ يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ دُوْنِكَ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ وَ لٰكِنْ مَّتَّعْتَهُمْ وَاٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى نَسُوا الذِّكْرَ‌ۚ وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًۢا بُوْرًا‏(18)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA MAA KAANA YAMBAGHEE LANAA AN NATTAKHEZA MIN DOONEKA MIN AWLEYAAA-A WA LAAKIM MATTA’TAHUM WA AABAAA-AHUM HATTAA NASUZ ZIKR, WA KAANOO QAWMAM BOORAA.\nThey will say, ‘Immaculate are You! It does not behoove us to take any wali in Your stead! But You provided for them and their fathers until they forgot the Reminder, and they were a ruined lot.’\nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْكُمْ بِمَا تَقُوْلُوْنَۙ فَمَا تَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ صَرْفًا وَّلَا نَصْرًا‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّظْلِمْ مِّنْكُمْ نُذِقْهُ عَذَابًا كَبِيْرًا‏(19)\nFAQAD KAZZABOOKUM BEMAA TAQOOLOONA, FAMAA TASTATEE-O’ONA SARFANW WA LAA NASRAA, WA MAN-Y YAZLIM MINKUM NOZIQHO A’ZAABAN KABEERAA.\nSo they will certainly impugn you in what you say, and you will neither be able to circumvent [punishment] nor find help, and whoever of you does wrong, We shall make him taste a terrible punishment.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّاۤ اِنَّهُمْ لَيَاْكُلُوْنَ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشُوْنَ فِى الْاَسْوَاقِ‌ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا بَعْضَكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ فِتْنَةً  ؕ اَتَصْبِرُوْنَ‌ۚ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ بَصِيْرًا‏(20)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA QABLAKA MENAL MURSALEENA ILLAA INNAHUM LAYAAKOLOONAT TA-A’AMA WA YAMSHOONA FIL ASWAAQ, WA JA-A’LNAA BA’ZAKUM LE-BA’ZIN FITNAH, ATASBEROON, WA KAANA RABBOKA BASEERAA.\nWe did not send any apostles before you but that they indeed ate food and walked in marketplaces. We have made you a [means of] test for one another, [to see] if you will be patient and steadfast, and your Lord is all-seeing.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ اَوْ نَرٰى رَبَّنَا ؕ لَقَدِ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَعَتَوْ عُتُوًّا كَبِيْرًا‏(21)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA LAA YARJOONA LEQAAA-ANAA LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYNAL MALAAA-EKATO AW NARAA RABBANAA, LAQADIS TAKBAROO FEE ANFOSEHIM WA A’TAW O’TUWWAN KABEERAA.\nThose who do not expect to encounter Us say, ‘Why have angels not been sent down to us, or why do we not see our Lord?’ Certainly, they are full of arrogance within their souls and have become terribly defiant.\nيَوْمَ يَرَوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ لَا بُشْرٰى يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُجْرِمِيْنَ وَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ حِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(22)\nYAWMA YARAWNAL MALAAA-EKATA LAA BUSHRAA YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MUJREMEENA WA YAQOOLOONA HIJRAM MAHJOORAA.\nThe day they will see the angels, there will be no good news for the guilty on that day, and they will say, ‘Keep off [from paradise]!’\nوَقَدِمْنَاۤ اِلٰى مَا عَمِلُوْا مِنْ عَمَلٍ فَجَعَلْنٰهُ هَبَآءً مَّنْثُوْرًا‏(23)\nWA QADIMNAA ELAA MAA A’MELOO MIN A’MALIN FA-JA-A’LNAAHO HABAAA-AM MANSOORAA.\nThen We shall attend to the works they have done and then turn them into scattered dust.\nاَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ يَوْمَئِذٍ خَيْرٌ مُّسْتَقَرًّا وَّاَحْسَنُ مَقِيْلًا‏(24)\nASHAABUL JANNATE YAWMA-EZIN KHAYRUM MUSTAQARRANW WA AHSANO MAQEELAA.\nOn that day the inhabitants of paradise will be in the best abode and an excellent resting place.\nوَيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ السَّمَآءُ بِالْغَمَامِ وَنُزِّلَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ تَنْزِيْلًا‏(25)\nWA YAWMA TASHAQQAQUS SAMAAA-O BIL-GHAMAAME WA NUZZELAL MALAAA-EKATO TANZEELAA.\nThe day when the sky with its clouds will be split open, and the angels will be sent down [in a majestic] descent,\nاَلْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْحَقُّ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ‌ؕ وَكَانَ يَوْمًا عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَسِيْرًا‏(26)\nAL-MULKO YAWMA-EZENIL HAQQO LIR-RAHMAAN, WA KAANA YAWMAN A’LAL KAAFEREENA A’SEERAA.\non that day true sovereignty will belong to the All-beneficent, and it will be a hard day for the faithless.\nوَيَوْمَ يَعَضُّ الظَّالِمُ عَلٰى يَدَيْهِ يَقُوْلُ يٰلَيْتَنِى اتَّخَذْتُ مَعَ الرَّسُوْلِ سَبِيْلًا‏(27)\nWA YAWMA YA-A’ZZUZ ZAALEMO A’LAA YADAYHE YAQOOLO YAA LAYTANIT TAKHAZTO MA-A’R RASOOLE SABEELAA.\nIt will be a day when the wrongdoer will bite his hands, saying, ‘I wish I had followed the Apostle’s way!\nيٰوَيْلَتٰى لَيْتَنِىْ لَمْ اَتَّخِذْ فُلَانًا خَلِيْلًا‏(28)\nYAA WAYLATAA LAYTANEE LAM ATTAKHIZ FOLAANAN KHALEELAA.\nWoe to me! I wish I had not taken so and so as a friend!\nلَقَدْ اَضَلَّنِىْ عَنِ الذِّكْرِ بَعْدَ اِذْ جَآءَنِىْ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ الشَّيْطٰنُ لِلْاِنْسَانِ خَذُوْلًا‏(29)\nLAQAD AZALLANEE A’NIZ ZIKRE BA’DA IZ JAAA-ANEE, WA KAANASH SHAYTAANO LIL-INSAANE KHAZOOLAA.\nCertainly he led me astray from the Reminder after it had come to me, and Satan is a deserter of man.’\nوَقَالَ الرَّسُوْلُ يٰرَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِى اتَّخَذُوْا هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ مَهْجُوْرًا‏(30)\nWA QAALAR RASOOLO YAA RABBE INNA QAWMIT TAKHAZOO HAAZAL QUR-AANA MAHJOORAA.\nAnd the Apostle will say, ‘O my Lord! Indeed my people consigned this Quran to oblivion.’\nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّا مِّنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‌ؕ وَكَفٰى بِرَبِّكَ هَادِيًا وَّنَصِيْرًا‏(31)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA LE-KULLE NABIYYIN A’DUWWAM MENAL MUJREMEEN, WA KAFAA BE-RABBEKA HAADEYANW WA NASEERAA.\nThat is how for every prophet We assigned an enemy from among the guilty, and your Lord suffices as helper and guide.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ جُمْلَةً وَّاحِدَةً‌  ‌ۛۚ كَذٰلِكَ ‌ۛۚ لِنُثَبِّتَ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ‌ وَرَتَّلْنٰهُ تَرْتِيْلًا‏(32)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAWLAA NUZZELA A’LAYHIL QUR-AANO JUMLATANW WAAHEDAH, KAZAALEK, LE-NOSABBETA BEHI FO-AADAKA WA RATTALNAAHO TARTEELAA.\nThe faithless say, ‘Why has not the Quran been sent down to him all at once?’ So it was, that We may strengthen your heart with it, and We have recited it [to you] in a measured tone.\nوَلَا يَاْتُوْنَكَ بِمَثَلٍ اِلَّا جِئْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَحْسَنَ تَفْسِيْرًا ؕ‏(33)\nWA LAA YAATOONAKA BE-MASALIN ILLAA JEANAAKA BIL-HAQQE WA AHSANA TAFSEERAA.\nThey do not bring you any representation but that We bring you the truth [in reply to them] and the best exposition.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُحْشَرُوْنَ عَلٰى وُجُوْهِهِمْ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(34)\nLAZEENA YOHSHAROONA A’LAA WOJOOHEHIM ELAA JAHANNAMA, OOLAAA-EKA SHARRUM MAKAANANW WA AZALLO SABEELAA.\nThose who will be mustered [fallen] on their faces toward hell, they are the worse situated and further astray from the [right] way.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلْنَا مَعَهٗۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ وَزِيْرًا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(35)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LNAA MA-A’HU AKHAAHO HAAROONA WAZEERAA.\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book and We made Aaron, his brother, accompany him as a minister.\nفَقُلْنَا اذْهَبَاۤ اِلَى الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَاؕ فَدَمَّرْنٰهُمْ تَدْمِيْرًاؕ‏(36)\nFA-QULNAZ HABAA ELAL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA, FA-DAMMARNAAHUM TADMEERAA.\nThen We said, ‘Let the two of you go to the people who have denied Our signs.’ Then We destroyed them utterly.\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ لَّمَّا كَذَّبُوا الرُّسُلَ اَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ وَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ لِلنَّاسِ اٰيَةً ‌ ؕ وَاَعْتَدْنَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ عَذَابًا اَ لِيْمًا ‌ۖ‌ ۚ‏(37)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIL LAMMAA KAZZABUR ROSOLA AGHRAQNAAHUM WA JA-A’LNAAHUM LIN-NAASE AAYAH, WA A-A’TADNAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nAnd Noah’s people, We drowned them when they impugned the apostles, and We made them a sign for mankind, and We have prepared for the wrongdoers a painful punishment.\nوَّعَادًا وَّثَمُوْدَا۟ وَ اَصْحٰبَ الرَّسِّ وَقُرُوْنًۢا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ كَثِيْرًا‏(38)\nWA A’ADANW WA SAMOODA WA ASHAABAR RASSE WA QOROONAM BAYNA ZAALEKA KASEERAA.\nAnd ‘Ad and Thamud, and the people of Rass, and many generations between them.\nوَكُلًّا ضَرَبْنَا لَهُ الْاَمْثَالَ‌ وَكُلًّا تَبَّرْنَا تَتْبِيْرًا‏(39)\nWA KULLAN ZARABNAA LAHUL AMSAAL, WA KULLAN TABBARNAA TATBEERAA.\nFor each of them We drew examples, and each We destroyed utterly.\nوَلَقَدْ اَتَوْا عَلَى الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْۤ اُمْطِرَتْ مَطَرَ السَّوْءِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا يَرَوْنَهَا ‌ۚ بَلْ كَانُوْا لَا يَرْجُوْنَ نُشُوْرًا‏(40)\nWA LAQAD ATAW A’LAL QARYATIL LATEE UMTERAT MATARAS SAW, AFALAM YAKOONOO YARAWNAHAA, BAL KAANOO LAA YARJOONA NOSHOORAA.\nCertainly they must have passed the town on which an evil shower was rained. Have they not seen it? Rather, they did not expect resurrection [to happen].\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْكَ اِنْ يَّتَّخِذُوْنَكَ اِلَّا هُزُوًا ؕ اَهٰذَا الَّذِىْ بَعَثَ اللّٰهُ رَسُوْلًا‏(41)\nWA EZAA RA-AWKA IN-Y YATTAKHEZOONAKA ILLAA HOZOWAA, AHAAZAL LAZEE BA-A’SAL LAAHO RASOOLAA.\nWhen they see you they just take you in derision: ‘Is this the one whom Allah has sent as an apostle!?\nاِنْ كَادَ لَيُضِلُّنَا عَنْ اٰلِهَتِنَا لَوْ لَاۤ اَنْ صَبَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ وَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ حِيْنَ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذَابَ مَنْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(42)\nIN KAADA LAYOZILLONAA A’N AALEHATENAA LAWLAA AN SABARNAA A’LAYHAA, WA SAWFA YA’LAMOONA HEENA YARAWNAL A’ZAABA MAN AZALLO SABEELAA.\nIndeed he was about to lead us astray from our gods, had we not stood firm by them.’ Soon they will know, when they sight the punishment, who is further astray from the [right] way.\nاَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تَكُوْنُ عَلَيْهِ وَكِيْلًا ۙ‏(43)\nARA-AYTA MANIT TAKHAZA ELAAHAHU HAWAAH, AFA-ANTA TAKOONO A’LAYHE WAKEELAA.\nHave you seen him who has taken his desire to be his god? Is it your duty to watch over him?\nاَمْ تَحْسَبُ اَنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ يَسْمَعُوْنَ اَوْ يَعْقِلُوْنَ‌ ؕ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا كَالْاَنْعَامِ‌ بَلْ هُمْ اَضَلُّ سَبِيْلًا‏(44)\nAM TAHSABO ANNA AKSARAHUM YASMA-O’ONA AW YA’QELOON, IN HUM ILLAA KAL-AN-A’AME BAL HUM AZALLO SABEELAA.\nDo you suppose that most of them listen or exercise their reason? They are just like cattle; indeed, they are further astray from the way.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ كَيْفَ مَدَّ الظِّلَّ‌ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ لَجَعَلَهٗ سَاكِنًا‌ ۚ ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَا الشَّمْسَ عَلَيْهِ دَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(45)\nALAM TARA ELAA RABBEKA KAYFA MADDAZ ZIL, WA LAW SHAAA-A LAJA-A’LAHU SAAKENAA, SUMMA JA-A’LNASH SHAMSA A’LAYHE DALEELAA.\nHave you not regarded how your Lord spreads the twilight? (Had He wished He would have made it stand still.) Then We made the sun a beacon for it.\nثُمَّ قَبَضْنٰهُ اِلَيْنَا قَبْضًا يَّسِيْرًا‏(46)\nSUMMA QABAZNAAHO ELAYNAA QABZAN-Y YASEERAA.\nThen We retract it toward Ourselves, with a gentle retracting.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِبَاسًا وَّالنَّوْمَ سُبَاتًا وَّجَعَلَ النَّهَارَ نُشُوْرًا‏(47)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LEBAASANW WAN NAWMA SOBAATANW WA JA-A’LAN NAHAARA NOSHOORAA.\nIt is He who made for you the night as a covering and sleep for rest and He made the day a recall to life.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ۚ وَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً طَهُوْرًا ۙ‏(48)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE ARSALAR REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY RAHMATEH, WA ANZALNAA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN TAHOORAA.\nAnd it is He who sends the winds as harbingers of His mercy, and We send down from the sky purifying water,\nلِّنُحْیِۦَ بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا وَّنُسْقِيَهٗ مِمَّا خَلَقْنَاۤ اَنْعَامًا وَّاَنَاسِىَّ كَثِيْرًا‏(49)\nLE-NOHYA BEHI BALDATAM MAYTANW WA NUSQEYAHU MIMMAA KHALAQNAA AN-A’AMANW WA ANAASIYYA KASEERAA.\nwith which We revive a dead country and provide water to many of the cattle and humans We have created.\nوَلَقَدْ صَرَّفْنٰهُ بَيْنَهُمْ لِيَذَّكَّرُوْا ‌ ۖ ا فَاَبٰٓى اَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ اِلَّا كُفُوْرًا‏(50)\nWA LAQAD SARRAFNAAHO BAYNAHUM LE-YAZZAKKAROO, FA-ABAA AKSARUN NAASE ILLAA KOFOORAA.\nCertainly We distribute it among them so that they may take admonition. But most people are only intent on ingratitude.\nوَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَبَعَثْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ قَرْيَةٍ نَّذِيْرًا ‌ۖ ‏(51)\nWA LAW SHEANAA LABA-A’SNAA FEE KULLE QARYATIN NAZEERAA.\nHad We wished, We would have sent a warner to every town.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ وَ جَاهِدْهُمْ بِهٖ جِهَادًا كَبِيْرًا‏(52)\nFALAA TOTE-I’L KAAFEREENA WA JAAHIDHUM BEHI JEHAADAN KABEERAA.\nSo do not obey the faithless, but wage a great jihad against them with it.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ مَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ هٰذَا عَذْبٌ فُرَاتٌ وَّهٰذَا مِلْحٌ‌ اُجَاجٌ ۚ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًا وَّحِجْرًا مَّحْجُوْرًا‏(53)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE MARAJAL BAHRAYNE HAAZAA A’ZBUN FORAATUNW WA HAAZAA MILHUN OJAAJ, WA JA-A’LA BAYNAHOMAA BARZAKHANW WA HIJRAM MAHJOORAA.\nIt is He who merged the two seas: this one sweet and agreeable, and that one briny and bitter, and between the two He set a barrier and a forbidding hindrance.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ مِنَ الْمَآءِ بَشَرًا فَجَعَلَهٗ نَسَبًا وَّ صِهْرًا‌ ؕ وَكَانَ رَبُّكَ قَدِيْرًا‏(54)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE KHALAQA MENAL MAAA-E BASHARAN FA-JA-A’LAHU NASABANW WA SEHRAA, WA KAANA RABBOKA QADEERAA.\nIt is He who created the human being from water, then invested him with ties of blood and marriage, and your Lord is all-powerful.\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَلَا يَضُرُّهُمْ‌ؕ وَكَانَ الْكَافِرُ عَلٰى رَبِّهٖ ظَهِيْرًا‏(55)\nWA YA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFA-O’HUM WA LAA YAZURROHUM, WA KAANAL KAAFERO A’LAA RABBEHI ZAHEERAA.\nThey worship besides Allah that which neither brings them any benefit nor causes them any harm, and the faithless one is ever an abettor against his Lord.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا‏(56)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA MOBASH-SHERANW WA NAZEERAA.\nWe did not send you except as a bearer of good news and as a warner.\nقُلْ مَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ سَبِيْلًا‏(57)\nQUL MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJRIN ILLAA MAN SHAAA-A AN-Y YATTAKHEZA ELAA RABBEHI SABEELAA.\nSay, ‘I do not ask you any reward for it, except that anyone who wishes should take the way to his Lord.’\nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِهٖ‌ ؕ وَكَفٰى بِهٖ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرَ ا‌ ۛۚ ۙ‏(58)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL HAYYIL LAZEE LAA YAMOOTO WA SABBEH BE-HAMDEH, WA KAFAA BEHI BE-ZONOOBE E’BAADEHI KHABEERAA.\nPut your trust in the Living One who does not die, and celebrate His praise. He suffices as one all-aware of the sins of His servants.\nاۨلَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ ‌ۛۚ اَلرَّحْمٰنُ فَسْئَلْ بِهٖ خَبِيْرًا‏(59)\nLAZEE KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SITTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMAS TAWAA A’LAL A’RSH, RAHMAANO FAS-AL BEHI KHABEERAA.\nHe, who created the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them in six days, and then settled on the Throne, the All-beneficent; so ask someone who is well aware about Him.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اسْجُدُوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ قَالُوْا وَمَا الرَّحْمٰنُ اَنَسْجُدُ لِمَا تَاْمُرُنَا وَزَادَهُمْ نُفُوْرًا ۩‏(60)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUS JODOO LIR-RAHMAANE QAALOO WA MAR RAHMAAN, ANASJODO LEMAA TAAMORONAA WA ZAADAHUM NOFOORAA.\nWhen they are told: ‘Prostrate yourselves before the All-beneficent,’ they say, ‘What is ‘‘the All-beneficent’’? Shall we prostrate ourselves before whatever you bid us?’ And it increases their aversion.\nتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ فِى السَّمَآءِ بُرُوْجًا وَّجَعَلَ فِيْهَا سِرٰجًا وَّقَمَرًا مُّنِيْرًا‏(61)\nTABAARAKAL LAZEE JA-A’LA FIS SAMAAA-E BOROOJANW WA JA-A’LA FEEHAA SERAAJANW WA QAMARAM MONEERAA.\nBlessed is He who appointed houses in the sky and set in it a lamp and a shining moon.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ خِلْفَةً لِّمَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يَّذَّكَّرَ اَوْ اَرَادَ شُكُوْرًا‏(62)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE JA-A’LAL LAYLA WAN NAHAARA KHILFATAL LEMAN ARAADA AN-Y YAZZAKKARA AW ARAADA SHOKOORAA.\nIt is He who made the night and the day alternate for someone who desires to take admonition, or desires to give thanks.\nوَعِبَادُ الرَّحْمٰنِ الَّذِيْنَ يَمْشُوْنَ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ هَوْنًا وَّاِذَا خَاطَبَهُمُ الْجٰهِلُوْنَ قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‏(63)\nWA E’BAADUR RAHMAANIL LAZEENA YAMSHOONA A’LAL ARZE HAWNANW WA EZAA KHAATABAHOMUL JAAHELOONA QAALOO SALAAMAA.\nThe servants of the All-beneficent are those who walk humbly on the earth, and when the ignorant address them, say, ‘Peace!’\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَبِيْتُوْنَ لِرَبِّهِمْ سُجَّدًا وَّقِيَامًا‏(64)\nWAL LAZEENA YABEETOONA LE-RABBEHIM SUJJADANW WA QEYAAMAA.\nThose who spend the night for their Lord, prostrating and standing [in worship].\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا اصْرِفْ عَنَّا عَذَابَ جَهَنَّمَ ‌ۖ  اِنَّ عَذَابَهَا كَانَ غَرَامًا ‌ۖ ‏(65)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAS RIF A’NNAA A’ZAABA JAHANNAM, INNA A’ZAABAHAA KAANA GHARAAMAA.\nThose who say, ‘Our Lord! Turn away from us the punishment of hell. Indeed its punishment is enduring.\nاِنَّهَا سَآءَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(66)\nINNAHAA SAAA-AT MUSTAQARRANW WA MOQAAMAA.\nIndeed it is an evil station and abode.’\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا لَمْ يُسْرِفُوْا وَلَمْ يَقْتُرُوْا وَكَانَ بَيْنَ ذٰلِكَ قَوَامًا‏(67)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ANFAQOO LAM YUSREFOO WA LAM YAQTOROO WA KAANA BAYNA ZAALEKA QAWAAMAA.\nThose who are neither wasteful nor tightfisted when spending, but balanced between these [two extremes].\nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَدْعُوْنَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ وَلَا يَقْتُلُوْنَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا يَزْنُوْنَ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ يَلْقَ اَثَامًا ۙ‏(68)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YAD-O’ONA MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA WA LAA YAQTOLOONAN NAFSAL LATEE HARRAMAL LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE WA LAA YAZNOON, WA MAN-Y YAF-A’L ZAALEKA YALQA ASAAMAA.\nThose who do not invoke another deity besides Allah, and do not kill a soul [whose life] Allah has made inviolable, except with due cause, and do not commit fornication. (Whoever does that shall encounter its retribution,\nيُضٰعَفْ لَهُ الْعَذَابُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَيَخْلُدْ فِيْهٖ مُهَانًا ۖ ‏(69)\nYOZAA-A’F LAHUL A’ZAABO YAWMAL QEYAAMATE WA YAKHLUD FEEHI MOHAANAA.\nthe punishment being doubled for him on the Day of Resurrection. In it he will abide in humiliation forever,\nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ عَمَلًاصَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ حَسَنٰتٍ‌ ؕ وَكَانَ اللّٰهُ غَفُوْرًا رَّحِيْمًا‏(70)\nILLAA MAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA A’MALAN SAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YOBADDELUL LAAHO SAYYE-AATEHIM HASANAAT, WA KAANAL LAAHO GHAFOORAR RAHEEMAA.\nexcept those who repent, attain faith, and act righteously. For such, Allah will replace their misdeeds with good deeds, and Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.\nوَمَنْ تَابَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاِنَّهٗ يَتُوْبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَتَابًا‏(71)\nWA MAN TAABA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-INNAHU YATOOBO ELAL LAAHE MATAABAA.\nAnd whoever repents and acts righteously indeed turns to Allah with due penitence).\nوَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَشْهَدُوْنَ الزُّوْرَۙ وَ اِذَا مَرُّوْا بِاللَّغْوِ مَرُّوْا كِرَامًا‏(72)\nWAL LAZEENA LAA YASH-HADOONAZ ZOORA, WA EZAA MARROO BIL-LAGHWE MARROO KERAAMAA.\nThose who do not give false testimony, and when they come upon frivolity, pass by with dignity.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَمْ يَخِرُّوْا عَلَيْهَا صُمًّا وَّعُمْيَانًا‏(73)\nWAL LAZEENA EZAA ZUKKEROO BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM LAM YAKHIRROO A’LAYHAA SUMMANW WA U’MYAANAA.\nThose who, when reminded of the signs of their Lord, do not turn a deaf ear and a blind eye to them.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَا هَبْ لَنَا مِنْ اَزْوَاجِنَا وَذُرِّيّٰتِنَا قُرَّةَ اَعْيُنٍ وَّاجْعَلْنَا لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِمَامًا‏(74)\nWAL LAZEENA YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA HAB LANAA MIN AZWAAJENAA WA ZURRIYYAATENAA QURRATA A-A’YONINW WAJ A’LNAA LIL-MUTTAQEENA EMAAMAA.\nAnd those who say, ‘Our Lord! Give us joy and comfort in our spouses and offspring, and make us imams of the Godwary.’\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُجْزَوْنَ الْغُرْفَةَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا وَيُلَقَّوْنَ فِيْهَا تَحِيَّةً وَّسَلٰمًا ۙ‏(75)\nOOLAAA-EKA YUJZAWNAL GHURFATA BEMAA SABAROO WA YOLAQQAWNA FEEHAA TAHIYYATANW WA SALAAMAA.\nThose shall be rewarded with sublime abodes for their patience and steadfastness, and they shall be met there with greetings and ‘Peace,’\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ حَسُنَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّا وَّمُقَامًا‏(76)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, HASONAT MUSTAQARRANW WA MOQAAMAA.\nto abide in them [forever], an excellent station and abode.\nقُلْ مَا يَعْبَؤُا بِكُمْ رَبِّىْ لَوْلَا دُعَآؤُكُمْ‌ۚ فَقَدْ كَذَّبْتُمْ فَسَوْفَ يَكُوْنُ لِزَامًا‏(77)\nQUL MAA YA’BA-O BEKUM RABBEE LAWLAA DO-A’AA-OKUM, FAQAD KAZZABTUM FASAWFA YAKOONO LEZAAMAA.\nSay, ‘Were it not for the sake of summoning you [to faith], what store my Lord would have set by you? But you impugned [me and my summons], so it will soon follow as a result.’",
  "merits": "Surah al-Furqan (The Criterion)\nThis Surah has 77 verses and it is ‘Makki’. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a person who recites this Surah will be taken to Jannah without questioning, provided he believes in the Day of Judgement and the Raising of the Dead (from the graves).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that Allah (s.w.t.) will never send His punishment upon any person who recites this Surah every night. The reciter of this Surah will also gain a highly status in the hereafter. The person who writes this Surah and keeps it in his possession will never be harmed by the vermin of this earth."
